<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2090" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀθῷος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θωά</span>, 
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θωιή</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>scot-free</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				672
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγὼ μὲν ἀ. ἅπασι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					18.125
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀθῴους καθιστάναι τινάς</span>
			to secure their <i>immunity</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				3.11
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀθῷον ἀφιέναι</span> Test.
			ap. eund.<i><span class="en">
				21.107
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἀπαλλάττειν</span> or
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-εσθαι</span> to get off
			<i>scot-free</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Sph.</u>
				254d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				6.4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπέρχεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Archipp.
					40
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαφυγεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					130
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. gen.,
				<i>free from</i> a thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πληγῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Nu.</u>
					1413
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἀδικημάτων</span>
			<i>unpunished for</i> offences, <i><span class="en">
				Lycurg.
				79
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				14.76
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>unharmed by</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀθῷος τῆς Φιλίππου . . δυναστείας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					18.270
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>not deserving punishment, guiltless</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ὁ κτείνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Democr.
					257
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. χερσί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Ps.</u>
					23(24).4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἀπὸ τοῦ αἵματος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ev.Matt.</u>
					27.24
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>causing no harm, harmless</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κίνδυνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					<u>Prooem.</u>
					26
				</span></i>
			. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀθῷος</span> distinguished by
			Gramm. from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄθωος</span>, <i>of Mt.
				Athos</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				285
			</span></i>, cf. Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				1.128
			</span></i>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
